mhash 0.9.9.9 (2008) does not build or install cleanly against modern
toolchains (GCC 14+ defaults to C23, where an old-style "()" declaration
means "(void)"). Two minimal fixes, both verified against the actual
consumer (WendzelNNTPd 2.2.0-alpha):

1. lib/mhash_int.h: the key-generation declarations were forced into an
   old-style empty-parameter branch by "#define EMPTY_PROTOTYPES 1",
   while the definitions in lib/keygen.c take real parameters - C23
   rejects every one of them ("conflicting types"). The correct full
   prototypes already exist in the #else branch of the same
   conditional, so drop the forced define.

2. include/mutils/mincludes.h: the installed public headers only
   include the generated mutils/mhash_config.h when the CONSUMER
   defines MUTILS_USE_MHASH_CONFIG - a macro third-party code does not
   know about. Without it the headers are not self-contained: uint8_t/
   uint32_t are unknown (mutils.h maps its word types onto them) and
   PROTOTYPES stays undefined, leaving old-style declarations in
   mutils/mhash.h that reject real call sites (e.g. WendzelNNTPd's
   configure conformance test "MHASH td = mhash_init(MHASH_SHA256)"
   fails with "too many arguments to function 'mhash_init'"). The
   generated mhash_config.h is installed with the headers, so include
   it unconditionally.

--- a/lib/mhash_int.h
+++ b/lib/mhash_int.h
@@ -33,11 +33,7 @@
 		      mutils_word32 block);
 
 void *hmac_mhash_end(MHASH thread);
-
 /* Key generation functions */
-
-#define EMPTY_PROTOTYPES 1
-
 #if defined(EMPTY_PROTOTYPES)
 
 mutils_error mhash_keygen();
--- a/include/mutils/mincludes.h
+++ b/include/mutils/mincludes.h
@@ -30,7 +30,11 @@
 #if !defined(__MINCLUDES_H)
 #define __MINCLUDES_H
 
-#if defined(MUTILS_USE_MHASH_CONFIG)
+/* mutils/mhash_config.h is generated and installed with the headers;
+   the public headers are not self-contained without it (the uint8_t/
+   uint32_t types behind the mutils_word8/word32 macros and the
+   PROTOTYPES switch for mutils/mhash.h). */
+#if 1
 #include <mutils/mhash_config.h>
 #endif
 
